# Requirements Traceability Matrix

Project: RoomRadar QC  
Purpose: Trace user and admin requirements to the application screens, backend code, data objects, and verification approach.

## Requirement Summary

| ID | Requirement | Priority | Source / Rationale |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| FR-01 | Users can view a home page that explains the purpose of RoomRadar QC and links to room search. | High | Public landing and navigation need |
| FR-02 | Users can search for available rooms by day, start time, end time, duration, and building. | High | Main student workflow |
| FR-03 | The system validates that required search fields are provided. | High | Prevent incomplete searches |
| FR-04 | The system validates that start time is before end time. | High | Prevent invalid availability ranges |
| FR-05 | Users can view available room results with room code, building, and availability information. | High | Main student output |
| FR-06 | Users can open a room detail page to view the room schedule for the selected day. | Medium | Helps students confirm conflicts |
| FR-07 | Search state is preserved during the current browser session. | Medium | Improves usability when navigating back from details |
| FR-08 | Admin users can log in with Firebase authentication. | High | Protects administrative features |
| FR-09 | Admin-only pages are protected from unauthenticated users. | High | Access control |
| FR-10 | Admin users can log out and return to the public experience. | Medium | Session control |
| FR-11 | Admin users can choose semester season and year for uploaded data. | High | Data organization by term |
| FR-12 | Admin users can upload a CSV file containing course and room information. | High | Schedule ingestion workflow |
| FR-13 | The backend stores semesters, rooms, and schedules in MySQL. | High | Persistent data storage |
| FR-14 | The backend can search for rooms that do not conflict with scheduled classes. | High | Core availability calculation |
| FR-15 | The backend can return a room's schedule for a selected day. | Medium | Room details support |
| FR-16 | The backend handles database connection errors with a clear API response. | Medium | Reliability and troubleshooting |
| NFR-01 | The application provides a responsive web interface. | Medium | Student/admin accessibility across devices |
| NFR-02 | The system uses CORS to allow the frontend to call backend APIs during development. | Medium | Frontend/backend integration |
| NFR-03 | Backend configuration can be controlled through environment variables. | Medium | Deployment flexibility |

